{number: 87}
{title: What a Friend We Have in Jesus}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] What a friend we have in Jesus,
[Bb] All our sins and griefs to [F] bear!
What a privilege to [C7] carry
[F] Everything to God in prayer!
[C7] Oh, what peace we often forfeit,
[F] Oh, what [Bb] needless pain we [F] bear,
All because we do not [Bb] carry
[F] Everything to [C7] God in [F] prayer!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Have we trials and temptations?
[Bb] Is there trouble any-[F] where?
We should never be dis-[C7] couraged,
[F] Take it to the Lord in prayer.
[C7] Can we find a friend so faithful,
[F] Who will [Bb] all our sorrows [F] share?
Jesus knows our every [Bb] weakness;
[F] Take it to the [C7] Lord in [F] prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Are we weak and heavy-laden,
[Bb] Cumbered with a load of [F] care?
Precious Savior, still our [C7] refuge
[F] Take it to the Lord in prayer.
[C7] Do thy friends despise, forsake thee?
[F] Take it [Bb] to the Lord in [F] prayer;
In His arms He’ll take and [Bb] shield thee,
[F] Thou wilt find a [C7] solace [F] there.
{end_of_verse}
